hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1284","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi and Mahmoud bin Khadash told us, saying: Jarir bin Abdul-Hamid told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal, and it is Ibn Yasaf, on the authority of Wahb ibn Al-Ajda’, on the authority of Ali, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “He should not pray after the afternoon prayer unless the sun has set.” \high white\"""""
"1285","From us, Abu Musa Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna, from us from Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Sufyan, and Shu’bah, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal, on the authority of Wahb bin The most appropriate, on the authority of Ali, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Do not pray after the afternoon prayer unless you pray while the sun is high.”"
"1286","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad told us, Ishaq Al-Azraq told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim, who is Ibn Damrah, on the authority of Ali, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, is the same as the hadith of Abu Musa. Sufyan said: I do not know whether it is in Mecca or elsewhere. Abu Bakr said: “This is a strange hadith. I heard Muhammad bin Yahya saying: Wahb bin Al-Ajdaa has had the name of Al-Jahlamah rise from him, and Al-Sha’bi also narrated from him, and Hilal bin Yassaf"
